"Once wish, one want,\nNo boast, no flaunt.\n\nWhen it all started, there was enthusiasm,\nCrests and troughs, came in real,\nFor once I write, with no sarcasm.\n\nMisjudged the bridge, joining the cities,\nThe concrete perhaps, wasn't that good,\nAll the bridge got, were un-understood atrocities.\n\nBoth the cities, had different governments,\nDifferent constitutions, differing weather,\nMight has freedom, might had internments.\n\nA chaotic city, the other's not,\nA city of lies, which the other don't like,\nA city of rigid rules, which caused the true gunshot.\n\nThe bridge got the bullet, the concrete was already weak,\nThe pilars started to crumble,\nThe other city was called a freak.\n\nRepair was possible, with a mild fuss. \nBut the shooting city had another bridge,\nTo a city with more business.\n\nThe repair seemed worthless then,\nSince the deals were already directed,\nLong before the bridge got shot, for the other bridge wasn't in the ken.\n\nThe future transactions, hold no meaning,\nIf the broken bridge, was less important to rebuild,\nThe chaotic city, 'll be joyed without repairing."